{
  // The body-class table (spec §8.1, §16; CH-05, CH-11, CH-12). One row per class; the table has room for fifteen, so a role
  // player can get its own class later. Every captain names one (`bodyClass` in data/characters); a role player that names
  // none wears its captain's. Ten ship, one per captain.
  //
  // Size in play: `groundReachFt` is the stand-up reach on a ball hit on the ground (a grounder, a bunt), `flyReachFt` on a
  // ball hit in the air (a fly, a liner, a pop) — authored, never measured off the mesh, so a tall class may reach less than a
  // short one. `contactWidthMul` multiplies the barrel's two half-extents along the bat (§5.2); the height is the zone's.
  // Weight: `accelSec` is rest → rated speed and `brakeSec` rated speed → rest on the response law (light ramps fast, heavy
  // slow; the rated speed is the Run sub-stat's), and `knockbackMul` multiplies the recoil a hard take costs (1.0 light →
  // 0.5 heavy, the Sluggers ladder). `motionStyle` names the class's takes in data/art/clips.json.
  //
  // Proposed numbers (docs/decisions/plan-characters.md, "Open numbers"): a trial until Jack accepts one.
